          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Lie differentiation
            is the process reverse to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            and more generally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-group"} smooth ∞-group
            to its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For the moment, for ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
                see at
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie%27s+three+theorems"} Lie's three theorems
            %li
              %p
                For
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+theory"} infinity-Lie theory
                see at
                %em
                  %a{:href => "synthetic+differential+infinity-groupoid#LieDifferentiation"} synthetic differential infinity-groupoid – Lie differentiation
                \.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A formalization of the notion Lie differentiation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            has been given in (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie
            ), inspired by and building on results discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} model structure for L-∞ algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ForDeformationContexts"} For deformation contexts
          %p
            We then specialize this to those
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+contexts"} deformation contexts
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeformationContext"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ForCohesiveContexts"} For cohesive contexts
          %p
            This is the context in which one has a natural formulation of ordinary Lie differentiation of ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            and its generalization to the Lie differentiation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groups"} smooth ∞-groups
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
            below for more.
          %h3#ForDeformationContexts For deformation contexts
          #DeformationContext.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+context"} deformation context
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_*
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable (∞,1)-category
              %li
                %p
                  it contains an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} initial object
            %p and
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  equipped with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Stab
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo *
                          %mi op
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\{E_\alpha \in Stab(Sp_*^{op})\}
                %p
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} opposite (∞,1)-category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Sp
                            %mo *
                            %mi op
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_*^{op}
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def. 1.1.3
            ) together with the assumption of a terminal object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo *
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_*^{op}
            stated on p.9 (and later implicialy used).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeformationContext"}
              is meant to be read as follows:
            %p
              We think of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_*
              as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
              in some
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E_\alpha\}_\alpha
              as a set of generating
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+points"} infinitesimally thickened points
              (points in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+geometry"} formal geometry
          %p
            The following construction generates the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jets"}> jets
            ” induced by the generating infinitesimally thickened points.
          #SmallObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+context"} deformation context
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sp_*, \{E_\alpha\}_\alpha)
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo *
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_*^{op}
                  is an
                  %strong elementary morphism
                  if it is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
                  to a map into
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo −
                            %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{\infty -n}E_\alpha
                  for some
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
                  and some
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo *
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_*^{op}
                  is a
                  %strong small morphism
                  if it is the composite of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finitely
                  many elementary morphisms.
            %p We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo *
                      %mi inf
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sp_*^{inf} \hookrightarrow Sp_*
            %p
              for the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              on those objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              for which the essentially unique map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to *
              is small.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def. 1.1.8
            )
          #FormalModuliProblem.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+context"} deformation context
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sp_*, \{E_\alpha\}_\alpha)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeformationContext"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+moduli+problems"} formal moduli problems
              over it is the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo *
                      %mi inf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp_*^{inf}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi FormalModuli
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo *
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo *
                      %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    FormalModuli^{Sp_*}
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    PSh_\infty(Sp_*^{inf})
            %p
              on those
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
